I have created a simple component using rc-input-number, render() as below

```
render() {
    return ((
      <div className="number-input">
        <InputNumber
          onChange={this.onChange}
          onKeyDown={this.onKeyDown}
          formatter={value => `${formatNumberToString(value)}`}
        />
      </div>
    ));
  }

```

```
// makes only number input possible and avoid all alphabets etc
onKeyDown(e) {
    const { keyCode } = e;
    // backspace / delete key / tab key
    if (keyCode === 8 || keyCode === 46 || keyCode === 9) {
      return true;
    }

    // arrow keys
    if (keyCode > 36 && keyCode < 41) {
      return true;
    }
    // allow number keys
    if (keyCode > 47 && keyCode < 58) {
      return true;
    }

    // allow only one dot in number
    if (keyCode === 190) {
      if (this.state.value.indexOf('.') === -1) {
        return true;
      }
    }

    e.preventDefault();
    return false;
  }

```
where formatNumberToString() adds thousand separator comma to the number simply.

It works nicely when i change the number in component using number keys, but as soon as the focus is lost, the value in component displays without commas. Focusing again does not show commas, until i press a key to change the value. Also pressing up and down keys when the input is empty causes the number to changes, but again no commas appear until i press a key to input directly. 

Using latest 4.0.12 in react project.

Any help appreciated... what am I doing wrong?

