I couldn't reproduce this in Safari on an iOS 18.1 simulator (all three fields from your video scroll into view as soon as the keyboard opens). Not sure if it's an 18.7 issue specifically, or Chrome. On iOS 26.5, Chrome also works for me.

1. Does Safari on your phone (same iOS 18.7 device) show the same problem on the demo?
2. Since you can reproduce it in your own app: try adding this debug overlay in it, then focus a field in Chrome and share the numbers it shows while the keyboard is open:

```js
const el = document.createElement('div');
el.style.cssText = 'position:fixed;top:0;left:0;z-index:99999;background:#000;color:#fff;font:14px monospace;padding:4px';
document.body.append(el);
setInterval(() => {
  el.textContent = `inner=${window.innerHeight} vv=${visualViewport.height} top=${visualViewport.offsetTop}`;
}, 300);
```

The keyboard detection relies on `window.innerHeight - visualViewport.height`, so those two numbers should tell us whether Chrome on iOS 18 reports the viewport differently for you.
